title: Calls for an Einheitsfront
subtitle: The SAPD has called on us and the USPD to reconcile and unite.
max-visits: 1
view-if: sapd_consolidated == 1 and sapd_r >= 5 and (nsdap_r + dnvp_r + unemployed >= 40)
new-page: true
tags: event
on-arrival: {! 
Q.uspd_refuse = 0;
Q.uspd_good_faith = 0;
Q.uspd_bad_faith = 0;

if (Q.uspd_leader != "Liebknecht") {
    if (Q.peoples_party = 0 && Q.uspd_relation >= 80) {
        Q.uspd_good_faith = 1;
    }
    if (Q.peoples_party = 1 || Q.uspd_relation < 80) {
        if ((Q.uspd_relation >= 0) || (Q.uspd_relation >= -50 && Q.peoples_party == 0)) {
            Q.uspd_bad_faith = 1;
        }
        else {
            Q.uspd_refuse = 1;
        }
    }
}
if (Q.uspd_leader == "Liebknecht") {
    if (Q.peoples_party = 0 && Q.uspd_relation >= 35) {
        Q.uspd_good_faith = 1;
    }
    if (Q.peoples_party = 1 && Q.uspd_relation >= 50) {
        Q.uspd_good_faith = 1;
    }
    else {
        if (Q.peoples_party = 1) {
            if (Q.uspd_relation >= 25) {
                Q.uspd_bad_faith = 1;
            }
            
        }
        if (Q.peoples_party = 0) {
            if (Q.uspd_relation >= 10) {
                Q.uspd_bad_faith = 1;
            }
            
        }
        else {
            Q.uspd_refuse = 1;
        }
    }
}
!}

The SAPD, enjoying in its recent growth, has launched a manifesto and program calling for the SPD and USPD to put aside their differences and convene in an SAPD arbitrated conference for the formation of an "Einheitsfront" of the workers. If we refuse, it may reflect badly, especially on our working class base, and give the SAPD more ammunition.

- @participate_good_faith_1: We will attend this conference as a means of reconciling with the USPD.
- @participate_good_faith_2: We will attend this conference as a means of reconciling with the USPD.
- @participate_good_faith_3: We will attend this conference as a means of reconciling with the USPD.
- @participate_bad_faith_1: We will attend this conference as a means of showing that reconciliation is impossible and hopeless.
- @participate_bad_faith_2: We will attend this conference as a means of showing that reconciliation is impossible and hopeless.
- @participate_bad_faith_3: We will attend this conference as a means of showing that reconciliation is impossible and hopeless.
- @refuse_1: Let the SAPD delude themselves with ideas of a united front, we will have no part in it.
- @refuse_2: Let the SAPD delude themselves with ideas of a united front, we will have no part in it.

@participate_good_faith_1
view-if: uspd_good_faith and not (uspd_bad_faith or uspd_refuse)
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 15; workers_sapd += 5; communist_coalition += 2; reformist_dissent += 10; neorevisionist_dissent += 15; left_strength += 10; left_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 10; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government

We agree to the idea and participate in the conference that the SAPD calls. To our surprise, the USPD not only participates but seems to do so in good faith with genuine interest in reconciliation [? if uspd_leader == "Liebknecht" : , undoubtedly under the influence of their Conciliator leadership ?]. Multiple agreements are reached, with the SAPD mediating many of the disputes, and the conference ends as a propaganda victory for the SAPD as well as what remains of our party's left-wing, and a noticeable increase in our relations with the USPD. Our party's right, as well as the country's, accuse us of collaboration with the Communists, and our relations with them have worsened.

Whether this will be the start of a new course or not remains to be seen.

@participate_good_faith_2
view-if: uspd_bad_faith and not (uspd_good_faith or uspd_refuse)
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government

We agree to the idea and participate in the conference that the SAPD calls. The USPD too participates, but seems to do so out of obligation rather than genuine goodwill. They, intransingent as always, set forth unreasonable demands, including [? if uspd_rectified_history = 0 : the expulsion of Noske from the party, ?][? if spd_toleration : the breaking of our toleration agreement, ?] the adoption of a more radically and revolutionary socialist agenda, and the breaking of ties with the Right.

- @accept_uspd: We will accept these demands.
- @refuse_uspd: We will refuse these outrageous demands.

@accept_uspd
choose-if: reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength < left_strength + center_strength + labor_strength
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD right would never allow this.
on-arrival: {! 
if (Q.uspd_rectified_history == 0) {
    Q.reformist_dissent += 12;
    Q.reformist_strength -= 2;
    Q.neorevisionist_dissent += 5; 
    Q.left_dissent -= 6; 
    Q.left_strength += 5; 
    Q.uspd_rectified_history = 1; 
    Q.z_relation -= 6; 
    Q.dvp_relation -= 6; 
    Q.ddp_relation -= 4; 
    Q.uspd_relation += 8*(1-Q.dissent); 
    Q.coalition_dissent += 1
}
if (Q.spd_toleration == 1) {
    Q.time_to_election = 3; 
    Q.spd_in_government = 0;
    Q.in_grand_coalition = 0; 
    Q.spd_toleration = 0; 
    Q.pro_republic -= 5; 
    Q.dvp_relation -= 5; 
    Q.z_relation -= 5;
}
if (Q.uspd_relation <= 40) {
    Q.uspd_relation = 50
}
if (Q.uspd_relation > 40) {
    Q.uspd_relation += 10
}
Q.z_relation -= 10;
Q.dvp_relation -= 15;
Q.communist_coalition = 3;
Q.reformist_dissent += 15;
Q.neorevisionist_dissent += 25;
Q.reformist_strength -= 10;
Q.neorevisionist_strength -= 15;
Q.left_strength += 25;
Q.left_dissent -= 10;
Q.ddp_relation -= 5;
Q.new_middle_spd *= 0.95;
Q.old_middle_spd *= 0.95;
Q.rural_spd *= 0.95;
Q.coalition_dissent += 1;
Q.workers_spd += (Q.workers_sapd*0.15)
Q.workers_sapd *= 0.85
!}
go-to: set_next_election_time if spd_toleration

Despite the opposition of the right-wing, we have agreed to the USPD's demands. This has shaken the party to its core, and caused a shift back towards the left. The USPD themselves are shocked, but quickly adapt to the new reality, ready to collaborate with the SPD though still viewing us with suspicion. The SAPD has meanwhile lost steam, with many rejoining the SPD.

@refuse_uspd
on-arrival: uspd_relation -= 10; workers_uspd -= 3; workers_spd += 1; workers_sapd += 2

Of course, we could never agree to such outrageous demands. The conference is a failure, and we blame the USPD for it. The SAPD continues to agitate for a united front, pointing to the failure of the SPD and USPD to cooperate as a reason to vote for the SAPD instead, but this thankfully doesn't effect us too much.

@participate_good_faith_3
view-if: uspd_refuse and not (uspd_good_faith or uspd_bad_faith)
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; workers_uspd -= 10; workers_sapd += 7; workers_spd += 3; unemployed_uspd -= 5; unemployed_sapd += 5; left_dissent -= 5; left_strength -= 5

We attend the SAPD conference, but are alone in doing so, with the USPD refusing. We accuse the USPD of being the reason for the failure of an Einheitsfront to take form, and our ties with the left and SAPD are somewhat repaired. The SAPD campaigns off of the USPD's failure to participate, taking yet more support away from them. The right-wing though, both of our party and as a whole, are nevertheless disgruntled by our participation.

@participate_bad_faith_1
view-if: uspd_good_faith and not (uspd_bad_faith or uspd_refuse)
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; workers_spd -= 2; workers_sapd += 2

We attend the SAPD conference, though not out of genuine will to reconcile but to try and weaken the SAPD's propaganda and prove reconciliation impossible. Frustratingly, the USPD has not done the same, and appear more reasonable than us. We put forward demands that we know the USPD can never accept, such as a full acceptance of the Weimar constitution, disbanding of the RFB into the Reichsbanner, and the leaving of the Comintern in favor of the Second International.

- @uspd_accept: The USPD shockingly accepts most of our demands.
- @uspd_refuse_offer: The USPD, as expected, refuses.

@uspd_accept
choose-if: uspd_leader == "Liebknecht" and uspd_relation >= 65 and communist_coalition >= 2 and pro_republic >= 80 and (rb_strength*rb_militancy >= rfb_strength*rfb_militancy)
unavailable-subtitle: The USPD would never accept any of these outrageous demands.

To our surprise, the Conciliator USPD leadership has shown willingness to accept most of these demands. They have proposed a counteroffer, to integrate the RFB under the Reichsbanner while still maintaining its operational independence, and to promise to operate by the methods outlined in the constitution, rather than endorsing the constitution itself. Of course, though, the demand they leave the Comintern is unacceptable so long as Moscow retains its iron grip over worldwide communist parties.

- @accept_counteroffer: We will accept this fair counteroffer.
- @reject_counteroffer: We will refuse this counteroffer, despite our accidental progress.

@accept_counteroffer
on-arrival: uspd_relation = 50 if uspd_relation < 40; uspd_relation += 10 if uspd_relation >= 40; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; dvp_relation -= 5; workers_sapd += 3; workers_uspd -= 5; unemployed_uspd -= 8; rfb_strength *= 0.6; rfb_militancy -= 0.25; rb_strength += (rfb_strength*0.8); rb_militancy += 0.05; communist_coalition += 5; pro_republic += uspd_votes

We may not have originally intended for reconciliation but this deal is too good to pass up. If the USPD is truly willing to abide by these, we will accept. This is a great day for German democracy.

@reject_counteroffer
subtitle: This will make us seem unreasonable.
on-arrival: uspd_relation -= 25; communist_coalition = 0; workers_spd -= 10; unemployed_spd -= 15; workers_sapd += 7; workers_uspd += 3; unemployed_sapd += 9; unemployed_uspd += 6; left_dissent += 15

We had no intention of reconciliation and that we got this far is a miracle, but that changes nothing. We refuse, and the SAPD and USPD label us as traitors.

@uspd_refuse_offer
on-arrival: uspd_relation -= 5; workers_spd -= 3; workers_uspd += 1; workers_sapd += 2; left_dissent += 5; reformist_strength += 5

As expected, the USPD refuses our outrageous demands. The conference is a failure, and the USPD and SAPD both blame us. The SAPD continues to agitate for a united front, pointing to the failure of the SPD and USPD to cooperate as a reason to vote for the SAPD instead, to some success.

@participate_bad_faith_2
view-if: uspd_bad_faith and not (uspd_good_faith or uspd_refuse)
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; unemployed_spd -= 3; unemployed_uspd -= 3; unemployed_sapd += 5; workers_sapd -= 3; uspd_relation -= 10

We attend the SAPD conference, though not out of genuine will to reconcile but to try and weaken the SAPD's propaganda and prove reconciliation impossible. The USPD does the same, and the conference is a disaster as the SAPD struggles to control heated arguments. Any hope of leftist unity that remained has died with this conference, which, although their attempts to paint both us and the USPD as unreasonable and them as an alternative, has taken much steam out of the SAPD's campaign as their goal of an Einheitsfront is seen as increasingly impossible.

@participate_bad_faith_3
view-if: uspd_refuse and not (uspd_good_faith or uspd_bad_faith)
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; z_relation -= 5 if z_party_leader != "Joos"; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; workers_uspd -= 10; workers_sapd += 7; workers_spd += 3; unemployed_uspd -= 5; unemployed_sapd += 5; left_dissent -= 5; left_strength -= 5

We attend the SAPD conference, but are alone in doing so, with the USPD refusing. We accuse the USPD of being the reason for the failure of an Einheitsfront to take form, and our ties with the left and SAPD are somewhat repaired. The SAPD campaigns off of the USPD's failure to participate, taking yet more support away from them. The right-wing though, both of our party and as a whole, are nevertheless disgruntled by our participation.

@refuse_1
view-if: (uspd_good_faith or uspd_bad_faith) and not uspd_refuse
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 10; workers_sapd += 4; workers_uspd += 1; unemployed_sapd += 6; unemployed_uspd += 4; uspd_relation -= 10; communist_coalition = 0; left_dissent += 10; old_middle_nsdap += 3; new_middle_nsdap += 3; sa_strength += 50; strife += 1

We refuse to attend, but, unfortunately for us, the USPD agrees and participates. Our support is weakened as we are the only ones absent, and the SAPD grows ever closer to the USPD. This has been a propaganda victory for the far-left, which leads to further far-right mobilization.

@refuse_2
view-if: uspd_refuse and not (uspd_good_faith or uspd_bad_faith)
on-arrival: workers_sapd += 15; unemployed_sapd += 15; workers_spd -= 5; workers_uspd -= 10; unemployed_spd -= 10; unemployed_uspd -= 5; uspd_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 10

We refuse to attend, as does the SAPD. They dedicate the conference to themselves, accompanied by many of our most leftwing members who attend anyway, as well as the USPD's rightmost. With both of our parties failing to entertain negotiations, the SAPD pushes itself as the only party able to forge an Einheitsfront of the workers, and this seems to work as they grow yet further.

